<http://data.silknow.org/object/010e01a5-d08a-3747-8db3-68712e88c9a2/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Upper Coat for a man\nEmbroidery on twill weave silk.\nYarkand; 19th century.\n2157(I.S.)\nCollected by Sir Douglas Forsyth, and given by him in 1875.\n\nOriginally styled as a Manchu lady's robe, this garment was re-tailored to become and upper coat for a man.  The side-fastening overlap across the front was removed and various alterations were made, such as the lengthening of the sleeves.  The added lengths were embroidered in a similar style, with fruiting branches and floral sprays, but in the chain-stitch and not the satin-stitch embroidery of China. []"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/010e01a5-d08a-3747-8db3-68712e88c9a2> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/eae30a46-2534-30d5-98d3-0fd4c5507c5c>
